accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  updated type  surgical pathology pathology report  ms 08  removed_accession_id  case  ms 08  removed_accession_id  removed_patient_name  daniel date taken  removed_date source care unit  adult medicine  cnt  126 meei mrn  removed_date path subspecialty service  breast 1 results to  lydecke b  sweet  m d  resident  gabrielle baker  m d  signed out by  ronald balassanian  m d             addended report             reason for addendum  1  additional immunohistochemistry results reason for addendum  2  additional fluorescence in situ hybridization  fish  results clinical data  the patient is a 60 year old woman with a suspicious mass seen on ultrasound and mammo in the right breast who presents for an us core biopsy  final diagnosis  a  breast  right   core biopsy  invasive adenocarcinoma of the breast  see note  note  sections of the core biopsy reveal an infiltrating tumor composed of nests and trabeculae with single file cords of tumor cells and associated desmoplastic stroma  the tumor cells are generally small with eccentrically placed nuclei and increased nucleus to cytoplasm ratio  an immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin is diffusely positive with only a minority of cells showing negative staining  the findings are compatible with invasive adenocarcinoma with predominately ductal differentiation  the results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  this case was presented at the mgh pathology breast conference on removed_date  by his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the final diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  gross description  received in formalin   labeled remove_patient_name  daniel  remove_mrn and  right breast   are 4 cylind