accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final  type  surgical pathology  pathology report   removed_accession_id   massachusetts general hospital  boston  ma  removed_case_id  tel  617  removed_date    surgical pathology report      accession     removed_accession_id    removed_patient_name  lesvi s   dob  removed_date  age  36   sex  f  mrn   removed_case_id   location  same day surgery unit  institution  mgh  date of operation  removed_date  date of accession  removed_date  reported  removed_date 14 51  results to   kevin s  hughes md      final pathologic diagnosis   a  breast  excision  left   low grade phyllodes tumor  3 5cm     see note      note  although many areas of this fibroepithelial lesion suggest fibroadenoma   it shows some architectural heterogeneity and variation in stromal cellularity   mostly low cellularity with focal areas of moderate cellularity   and mild  stromal cytologic atypia  mitotic activity can be found throughout the lesion   it is mostly low  less than 1 per 10 hpf   but is focally up to 3 per 10 hpf   there are a few areas with well developed fronds projecting into cystically  dilated ducts  these overall features indicate a low grade phyllodes tumor   the lesion is well circumscribed with a non infiltrative border  there is no  stromal overgrowth and no heterologous elements  in a three tiered  classification system for phyllodes tumors  benign  borderline  and malignant    this tumor would fall into the benign category  the tumor extends to the inked  margin in a few small foci        electronically signed out by kristina m braaten md       resident pathologist   jason f solus md      by his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the final diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       clinical history  36 year old female with left breast mass  consistent with fibroadenoma on core  biopsy in  removed_case_id   but clinically growing